{"schema_version":"m7_decision_relation.v2","note_id":"ZECH-PARENT-13","book":"Zech","relation_type":"named_zechariah_macro_parent_with_context_hydration","parent_span":"Zech.14.1-Zech.14.21","parent_literary_form":"day_oracle_sequence_and_holiness_coda_parent","children":["M7_sol-Zech-033","M7_sol-Zech-034","M7_sol-Zech-035","M7_sol-Zech-036","M7_sol-Zech-037"],"child_spans":["Zech.14.1-Zech.14.5","Zech.14.6-Zech.14.11","Zech.14.12-Zech.14.15","Zech.14.16-Zech.14.19","Zech.14.20-Zech.14.21"],"rationale":"day_oracle_sequence_and_holiness_coda_parent preserves the named Zech.14.1-Zech.14.21 context for its selected local forms.","mandatory_hydration":true,"boundary_authority":false,"non_authorizing":true}
{"schema_version":"m7_decision_relation.v2","note_id":"Zech-D01","book":"Zech","relation_type":"preserved_specialist_dissent_without_forced_consensus","case":"Zech.3.1-Zech.3.10","children":["M7_sol-Zech-006"],"selected_spans":["Zech.3.1-Zech.3.10"],"alternative_spans":["Zech.3.1-Zech.3.5","Zech.3.6-Zech.3.10"],"rationale":"The solemn-assurance verb plus saying formula at 3:6 can support a separately retrievable charge-and-sign unit. The boss rejects surfacing it because the courtroom, addressee, and symbolic logic remain open, but preserves the split as the principal route dissent.","appellant_role":"original_language_translation_specialist","appellant_status":"preserved_principal_dissent_no_forced_consensus","appeal_id":null,"boundary_authority":false,"forced_consensus":false,"non_authorizing":true}
{"schema_version":"m7_decision_relation.v2","note_id":"Zech-D02","book":"Zech","relation_type":"preserved_specialist_dissent_without_forced_consensus","case":"Zech.12.10-Zech.13.1","children":["M7_sol-Zech-030"],"selected_spans":["Zech.12.10-Zech.13.1"],"alternative_spans":["Zech.12.10-Zech.12.14","Zech.13.1-Zech.13.6"],"rationale":"The samekh after 12:14, chapter boundary, and fountain-to-purification association could place 13:1 with 13:2-6. The boss instead treats 13:1 as the cleansing resolution and 13:2 as the stronger new action onset, while preserving the alternate presentation and held-treatment request.","appellant_role":"prophetic_literary_form_primary","appellant_status":"preserved_disposition_and_boundary_dissent_no_active_appeal","appeal_id":null,"boundary_authority":false,"forced_consensus":false,"non_authorizing":true}
{"schema_version":"m7_decision_relation.v2","note_id":"Zech-D03","book":"Zech","relation_type":"preserved_specialist_dissent_without_forced_consensus","case":"Zech.2.6-Zech.2.13","children":["M7_sol-Zech-005"],"selected_spans":["Zech.2.6-Zech.2.13"],"alternative_spans":["Zech.2.6-Zech.2.9","Zech.2.10-Zech.2.13"],"rationale":"Internal paragraph turns and the Zion song restart support two children, but speaker and pronoun pressure would make the seam reading-sensitive. The whole proclamation stays active under the 2:1-13 parent.","appellant_role":"original_language_translation_specialist","appellant_status":"preserved_counterevidence_not_active_appeal","appeal_id":null,"boundary_authority":false,"forced_consensus":false,"non_authorizing":true}
{"schema_version":"m7_decision_relation.v2","note_id":"Zech-D04","book":"Zech","relation_type":"preserved_specialist_dissent_without_forced_consensus","case":"Zech.4.1-Zech.4.14","children":["M7_sol-Zech-007"],"selected_spans":["Zech.4.1-Zech.4.14"],"alternative_spans":["Zech.4.1-Zech.4.5","Zech.4.6-Zech.4.10","Zech.4.11-Zech.4.14"],"rationale":"Word-event formulas and the paragraph after 4:7 expose embedded oracle seams. The resumed questions about the same olive configuration keep those words inside the complete vision.","appellant_role":"prophetic_literary_form_primary","appellant_status":"preserved_counterevidence_not_active_appeal","appeal_id":null,"boundary_authority":false,"forced_consensus":false,"non_authorizing":true}
{"schema_version":"m7_decision_relation.v2","note_id":"Zech-D05","book":"Zech","relation_type":"preserved_specialist_dissent_without_forced_consensus","case":"Zech.7.1-Zech.8.23","children":["M7_sol-Zech-012","M7_sol-Zech-013","M7_sol-Zech-014","M7_sol-Zech-015","M7_sol-Zech-016","M7_sol-Zech-017","M7_sol-Zech-018","M7_sol-Zech-019"],"selected_spans":["Zech.7.1-Zech.7.3","Zech.7.4-Zech.7.7","Zech.7.8-Zech.7.14","Zech.8.1-Zech.8.8","Zech.8.9-Zech.8.13","Zech.8.14-Zech.8.17","Zech.8.18-Zech.8.19","Zech.8.20-Zech.8.23"],"alternative_spans":["Zech.7.1-Zech.7.7","Zech.7.8-Zech.7.14","Zech.8.1-Zech.8.17","Zech.8.18-Zech.8.23"],"rationale":"Question-answer and reversal logic favor larger retrieval blocks, but renewed word-events, distinct rhetorical functions, and paragraph closures support the selected dependent children with full inquiry-response hydration.","appellant_role":"canonical_relations_retrieval_premortem_primary","appellant_status":"preserved_larger_route_alternative_not_active_appeal","appeal_id":null,"boundary_authority":false,"forced_consensus":false,"non_authorizing":true}
{"schema_version":"m7_decision_relation.v2","note_id":"Zech-D06","book":"Zech","relation_type":"preserved_specialist_dissent_without_forced_consensus","case":"Zech.9.9-Zech.9.17","children":["M7_sol-Zech-021","M7_sol-Zech-022"],"selected_spans":["Zech.9.9-Zech.9.10","Zech.9.11-Zech.9.17"],"alternative_spans":["Zech.9.9-Zech.9.17"],"rationale":"No paragraph break and sustained Zion address can support one royal-restoration movement. The direct-address and action reset at 9:11 supports two children, while mandatory hydration blocks isolating the arrival line.","appellant_role":"original_language_translation_specialist","appellant_status":"preserved_larger_unit_dissent_not_active_appeal","appeal_id":null,"boundary_authority":false,"forced_consensus":false,"non_authorizing":true}
{"schema_version":"m7_decision_relation.v2","note_id":"Zech-D07","book":"Zech","relation_type":"preserved_specialist_dissent_without_forced_consensus","case":"Zech.11.1-Zech.11.17","children":["M7_sol-Zech-026","M7_sol-Zech-027","M7_sol-Zech-028"],"selected_spans":["Zech.11.1-Zech.11.3","Zech.11.4-Zech.11.14","Zech.11.15-Zech.11.17"],"alternative_spans":["Zech.11.1-Zech.11.14","Zech.11.15-Zech.11.17"],"rationale":"The shepherd wail anticipates the enactment and could join it as a prelude. Form, voice, paragraph closure, and the command at 11:4 instead distinguish lament from the first sign-act.","appellant_role":"prophetic_literary_form_primary","appellant_status":"preserved_larger_route_alternative_not_active_appeal","appeal_id":null,"boundary_authority":false,"forced_consensus":false,"non_authorizing":true}
{"schema_version":"m7_decision_relation.v2","note_id":"Zech-D08","book":"Zech","relation_type":"preserved_specialist_dissent_without_forced_consensus","case":"Zech.12.1-Zech.12.9","children":["M7_sol-Zech-029"],"selected_spans":["Zech.12.1-Zech.12.9"],"alternative_spans":["Zech.12.1-Zech.12.6","Zech.12.7-Zech.12.9"],"rationale":"The paragraph after 12:6 and save-Judah-first turn at 12:7 support a child seam. The latter verses complete the same siege-defense movement, so the boss keeps the larger oracle.","appellant_role":"original_language_translation_specialist","appellant_status":"preserved_counterevidence_not_active_appeal","appeal_id":null,"boundary_authority":false,"forced_consensus":false,"non_authorizing":true}
{"schema_version":"m7_decision_relation.v2","note_id":"Zech-D09","book":"Zech","relation_type":"preserved_specialist_dissent_without_forced_consensus","case":"Zech.14.1-Zech.14.21","children":["M7_sol-Zech-033","M7_sol-Zech-034","M7_sol-Zech-035","M7_sol-Zech-036","M7_sol-Zech-037"],"selected_spans":["Zech.14.1-Zech.14.5","Zech.14.6-Zech.14.11","Zech.14.12-Zech.14.15","Zech.14.16-Zech.14.19","Zech.14.20-Zech.14.21"],"alternative_spans":["Zech.14.1-Zech.14.11","Zech.14.12-Zech.14.21"],"rationale":"Day continuity supports two large halves, but the cosmic-condition reset at 14:6, plague onset at 14:12, survivor-pilgrimage turn at 14:16, and holiness coda at 14:20 support five hydrated movements.","appellant_role":"canonical_relations_retrieval_premortem_primary","appellant_status":"preserved_larger_route_alternative_not_active_appeal","appeal_id":null,"boundary_authority":false,"forced_consensus":false,"non_authorizing":true}
{"schema_version":"m7_decision_relation.v2","note_id":"ZECH-ACTIVE-APPEAL-HEBREW-3-1-10","book":"Zech","relation_type":"active_post_ruling_appeal","case":null,"children":["M7_sol-Zech-006"],"selected_spans":null,"alternative_spans":["Zech.3.1-Zech.3.5","Zech.3.6-Zech.3.10"],"rationale":"Zech.3.1-5 completes the courtroom-reclothing action, including the speaker-sensitive wa-omar at 3:5. Zech.3.6 then supplies a substantial formal onset: wayyaad malakh-YHWH lemor introduces a solemn charge, followed by conditional clauses and the sign, Branch, and stone oracle through 3:10. The unchanged addressee, open tableau, absence of a Masoretic paragraph break, and dependence of the sign on the reclothing are serious counterevidence, so the requested split remains medium-confidence rather than categorical.","appellant_role":"original_language_translation_specialist","appellant_status":"open_deferred_human_or_external_ai","appeal_id":"Zech-Hebrew-A01","boundary_authority":false,"forced_consensus":false,"non_authorizing":true}
{"schema_version":"m7_decision_relation.v2","note_id":"ZECH-ACTIVE-APPEAL-LITERARY-12-10-13-1","book":"Zech","relation_type":"active_post_ruling_appeal","case":null,"children":["M7_sol-Zech-030"],"selected_spans":null,"alternative_spans":["Zech.12.10-Zech.12.14","Zech.13.1 dependent purification opening"],"rationale":"The larger surface is defensible because 13:1 repeats the same-day frame, names the same David-house and Jerusalem audience, and supplies cleansing after supplication and mourning. The competing treatment remains comparably defensible because a WLC-family samekh follows 12:14, the lament catalogue closes there, and 13:1 changes action from mourning to an opened fountain before the renewed removal saying at 13:2.","appellant_role":"prophetic_literary_form_primary","appellant_status":"open_deferred_human_or_external_ai","appeal_id":"T560-LIT-APPEAL-ZECH-12-10-13-1-TREATMENT","boundary_authority":false,"forced_consensus":false,"non_authorizing":true}
